<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47960" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέ-ᾱμα</span></b> , 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θέημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεάομαι</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sight,
				spectacle</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Semon.
				7.67
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				306
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				783
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1716
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ τις ὀρχοῖτ᾽ εὖ, θέαμ᾽ ἦν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.Com.
					130
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάθημα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.39
			</span></i>; freq. of a sight which gives pleasure, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεάματα καὶ ἀκροάματα ἥδιστα παρέχεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					2.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρχήσεις καὶ θεάματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mus.</u>
					p.26
				</span></i>
			 K.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμπλήσθητε τοῦ καλοῦ
			θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				440a
			</span></i>; but also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. δυσθέατον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					69
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				992
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑπτὰ θ.</span> the seven
				<i>wonders of the world</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				14.2.5
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.983e
			</span></i>: sg., of a marvellously engraved ring, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				17.1
			</span></i>.</div>
